# No logs at all: Caddy's own lines can name a client's address and a request's path (an error
# when the API cannot be reached), and the privacy policy promises no access logs and no stored
# IP addresses (deploy/README.md, "Looking after it"); the site has no `log` directive, so no
# access log either. To debug certificate problems, remove this block knowingly, then restore it.
{
	log {
		output discard
	}
}

# TLS certificates are obtained automatically; WebSocket upgrades are proxied as well.
{$API_DOMAIN} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy api:8080
}
